        "original_id": "4d6f869e-2c1d-5e03-88f9-a17126bff860",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: China\n- Events: Cricket fighting\n- Concepts: Blood sports\n- Topics: Crickets as pets, cricket breeding and selection, Chinese imperial court\n\nFacts:\n- Cricket fighting in China dates back more than 1,000 years to the Tang Dynasty.\n- In the early 12th century, Chinese people began holding cricket fights.\n- Cricket fighting is a blood sport involving fights between male crickets.\n- During the Qing dynasty, the Chinese art of selecting and breeding the finest fighting crickets was perfected.\n- The Chinese imperial court kept a monopoly on selecting and breeding the finest fighting crickets until the beginning of the 19th century.",
